  "summary": "A technique for correcting or adding details to frescoes using paint on dry plaster.",
  "description": "Involves applying pigments mixed with binders like glue or egg tempera onto dry plaster, used to fix mistakes or add details after the initial fresco dried. This technique was commonly employed throughout Renaissance periods as a corrective measure when buon fresco sections required refinement.",
